    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <h3>Resale vs. Retail Price Distribution</h3>
      <canvas id="priceDensityChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight-box">
    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> The market is moderately profitable with a 61.3% premium rate. However, the profit distribution is bimodal — Deadstock items drive significant premiums (avg +$264) while Used items consistently sell below retail (avg −$58). The median profit of $35.27 versus the mean of $82.06 reveals a right-skewed distribution where a subset of high-premium Deadstock sales pull the average upward.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Section 2: Model & Colorway Analysis -->
<div class="section">
  <h2><span class="num">2</span> Performance by Shoe Model &amp; Colorway</h2>

  <div class="chart-row two">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <h3>Average Profit Margin by Model</h3>
      <canvas id="modelProfitChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <h3>Average Profit Margin by Colorway</h3>
      <canvas id="colorwayProfitChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row two">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <h3>Model Performance Matrix</h3>
      <canvas id="modelScatterChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <h3>Premium Rate &amp; Volume by Model</h3>
      <canvas id="modelPremiumChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Transactions</th><th>Avg Retail</th><th>Avg Resale</th><th>Avg Profit</th><th>Margin %</th><th>Premium Rate</th><th>Avg Days</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Air Jordan 11 Retro</td><td>973</td><td>$227.48</td><td>$327.31</td><td class="pos">$99.84</td><td>43.9%</td><td>63%</td><td>21.4</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Air Jordan 4 Retro</td><td>1,044</td><td>$217.49</td><td>$313.25</td><td class="pos">$95.76</td><td>44.0%</td><td>62%</td><td>22.8</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Air Jordan 3 Retro</td><td>1,037</td><td>$205.03</td><td>$287.82</td><td class="pos">$82.79</td><td>40.4%</td><td>59%</td><td>22.3</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Air Jordan 1 High</td><td>926</td><td>$180.33</td><td>$262.18</td><td class="pos">$81.85</td><td>45.3%</td><td>62%</td><td>22.7</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Air Jordan 1 Low</td><td>1,020</td><td>$125.36</td><td>$175.88</td><td class="pos">$50.52</td><td>40.3%</td><td>60%</td><td>23.1</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Colorway</th><th>Transactions</th><th>Avg Retail</th><th>Avg Resale</th><th>Avg Profit</th><th>Margin %</th><th>Premium Rate</th><th>Avg Days</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Pine Green</td><td>566</td><td>$189.16</td><td>$278.39</td><td class="pos">$89.23</td><td>46.4%</td><td>61%</td><td>22.7</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Military Blue</td><td>553</td><td>$192.28</td><td>$279.83</td><td class="pos">$87.55</td><td>44.7%</td><td>63%</td><td>22.2</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Chicago</td><td>564</td><td>$190.73</td><td>$276.33</td><td class="pos">$85.60</td><td>44.6%</td><td>62%</td><td>23.4</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sail</td><td>548</td><td>$189.17</td><td>$273.61</td><td class="pos">$84.44</td><td>45.3%</td><td>64%</td><td>22.2</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Lost &amp; Found</td><td>585</td><td>$193.75</td><td>$276.94</td><td class="pos">$83.19</td><td>41.9%</td><td>60%</td><td>22.5</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mocha</td><td>535</td><td>$190.93</td><td>$272.45</td><td class="pos">$81.52</td><td>42.4%</td><td>61%</td><td>22.9</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Concord</td><td>547</td><td>$191.21</td><td>$272.06</td><td class="pos">$80.85</td><td>42.7%</td><td>62%</td><td>21.6</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bred</td><td>542</td><td>$190.89</td><td>$267.43</td><td class="pos">$76.55</td><td>40.8%</td><td>62%</td><td>21.7</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Black Cat</td><td>560</td><td>$192.30</td><td>$261.64</td><td class="pos">$69.34</td><td>35.7%</td><td>58%</td><td>23.0</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="insight-box">
    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Air Jordan 11 Retro leads in absolute profit ($99.84 avg), while the AJ1 High delivers the highest margin percentage (45.3%) due to its lower retail base. Pine Green is the top-performing colorway with $89.23 average profit and a 46.4% margin. Black Cat underperforms at $69.34 profit and the lowest premium rate (58%). AJ1 Low generates the weakest absolute returns ($50.52 avg profit) due to its lower MSRP ($125 retail).
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Section 3: Condition Impact -->
<div class="section">
  <h2><span class="num">3</span> Impact of Shoe Condition on Resale Value</h2>

  <div class="chart-row three">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <h3>Avg Profit by Condition</h3>
      <canvas id="conditionProfitChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <h3>Premium Rate by Condition</h3>
      <canvas id="conditionPremiumChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
